module tasks.`2026-11-22-svg-loop-pinned-chrome`

task SvgLoopPinnedChrome {
  title "svg-loop gate depends on the installed Chrome version; pin the reference browser"
  verify $ make svg-loop
  paths "crates/bboxy450-svg", "Makefile", "scripts", ".gitignore"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; report what you removed. ROLE: EXECUTOR.

    ## Gap (Oracle audit of main 647d97ab8, 2026-11-22)
    `make svg-loop` exits 2: `ValueError: frozen reference advisory set changed` (`crates/bboxy450-svg/review.py:108`). The only difference: `matplotlib-scatter / 1x` is now over the vector budget (changed fraction 0.006159478) and is not in `fixtures/advisories.json`.
    Cause: the reference browser is not pinned. `references.py:181` and `capture.mjs:27` default to `/Applications/Google Chrome.app` (157.0.8103.80 on this machine); the frozen corpus records `Chrome/158.0.8127.37`. The gate's verdict depends on whichever Chrome the machine auto-updated to.

    ## Do
    1. Pin the reference browser the way the exporters are pinned: a Make-managed, hash-checked Chrome for Testing / chrome-headless-shell of the exact recorded version (158.0.8127.37 unless the spec's frozen evidence says otherwise), arm64 macOS, machine-local under the target dir, no global install, no operator prompt. `CHROME` override stays for explicit experiments only and is recorded in results.
    2. The loop refuses to compare against a frozen corpus when the browser version differs from the recorded one, with a message naming both versions, instead of reporting a changed advisory set.
    3. Do not widen budgets or edit the frozen advisory set. Re-run `make svg-loop` on the pinned browser; it must exit 0 with the frozen set unchanged.
    Every headless Chrome run passes `--use-mock-keychain --password-store=basic` and a private user-data-dir.

    4. **Second red full gate on main (Oracle audit):** `make test-parity` exits 2 on `scripts/test-landing.py` `GateReceiptTests.test_real_ci_entrypoint_binds_success_and_does_not_certify_failure` (`ValueError: substring not found` at line 1657). Cause: `8213133a7` made `make test-real-sessions` run only when `SESSIONS_DIR` is set (`scripts/ci-local.sh:120`), but the test still requires that stage in its ordered stage list. Update the test to match the opt-in contract: assert the default CI omits `test-real-sessions`, and that it is present and ordered when `SESSIONS_DIR` is set. Reproduce first: `python3 scripts/test-landing.py GateReceiptTests.test_real_ci_entrypoint_binds_success_and_does_not_certify_failure`.
    After both fixes, run `make test-parity` once (detached) on your final commit and report its exit.

    5. **Document corpus repair (Oracle ruling, answering your block):** `crates/bbt-doc/tests/corpus.rs:337` `real_corpus_links_numeric_handles_and_legacy_ledger_anchors_resolve` fails because 11 task records pushed in `6307f306c` quote status pills (`[[Passed]]`, `[[Blocked]]`, ...). Pills are a documented renderer feature, not links. In `link_targets` (corpus.rs:263) skip a `WikiLink` whose target `bbt_ui_model::emphasis::pill(target)` classifies as a pill; that classifier is the one home of the vocabulary. Do not edit the records. Add a fixture line with a pill beside a real broken link: the pill passes, the broken link still fails. Then refresh `make test-parity` once and land.

    ## Land
    Long commands detached with exit code to a file. `make land`. Report at reports/2026-11-22-svg-loop-pinned-chrome.den, then `task_report`.


    ## Report from seat:01M82JAGV0RX5ZC33EVF8XBX1B

    The SVG loop passed with pinned Chrome for Testing 158.0.8127.37, 216 native captures, and all 30 frozen advisories. Removed the installed-Chrome fallbacks and the unconditional saved-session assertion. The opt-in fixture, license gate and 997-model formal gate passed. The detached parity gate exited 2 after 2,903 passes because the document corpus treats existing status pills as unresolved links. Landing is blocked. Assign the document corpus repair so parity can be refreshed. The signed commit and clean worktree are retained.

    ```json
    {
      "op_id": "01M82X342NTCE2M71MYKBT6NF3",
      "commit": "65242bcdd535284ed7948d7e9d19dba2a82ef36c",
